cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  mpc-cbf: Discrete-time MPC with control barrier function
  constraints, with a tube-MPC-CBF extension
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Eimaan
    given-names: Ali
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-15'
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: https://github.com/Ali-Eiman/mpc-cbf
abstract: >-
  A single-agent safety-critical predictive controller in C++/acados and Python.
  Discrete-time control barrier function constraints are imposed along an MPC
  prediction horizon (Zeng, Zhang and Sreenath, ACC 2021), optionally with the
  decay rate as a decision variable (Zeng, Li and Sreenath, CDC 2021), plus a
  tube-MPC-CBF extension that tightens every constraint by an offline robust
  positively invariant set so the safety guarantee holds for the true state
  under bounded disturbance. Both source papers are reproduced figure by
  figure, with the matched values, tolerances and deviations recorded.
keywords:
  - control barrier function
  - model predictive control
  - safety-critical control
  - robust MPC
  - tube MPC
  - acados
  - ROS 2
